  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1: Trending humid with heavy downpours and \nlocalized flash flooding possible Wednesday into the weekend\n\nAfter a very nice/refreshing start to the week, deep moisture \nsurge of high pwats within a return SW flow will spell an \nincreased risk of heavy drenching downpours and localized flash \nflooding Wednesday into the upcoming weekend. WPC continues to \nshow broad marginal risks of excessive rain (ERO) given the \nuncertainty in the location of heavy rainfall. Conditions will \nbe warm and quite sticky/humid with dewpoints in the 65-75F \nrange; muggy nights 5-10+ degrees above the historical average.",
